meta {
  name: 32 Update Overall Result
  type: http
  seq: 32
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/overall-result/{{resultParamId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "templateId": "{{overallResultTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Apply an Overall Result template to ONE result parameter on a report, or
  edit that parameter's already-applied content in place — two mutually
  exclusive actions on the same endpoint, distinguished by which single field
  is sent.

  ⚠️ Changed 2026-09-22: this is now per-PARAMETER, not per-report.
  `resultParamId` (a `LabTestResultParam.id`) is a required path segment.
  Each parameter on a report holds its own independently-applied result — a
  test with several parameters (e.g. Bilirubin/SGOT/SGPT under Liver
  Function Test), each tagged into its own Overall Result group, can each
  have a DIFFERENT template/content applied. Calling this for one
  `resultParamId` never touches any other parameter's applied result on the
  same report. (Previously this endpoint had no `resultParamId` and applied
  to the whole report — that shared, single-slot design is what this change
  replaces; see `LabReportOverallResult` model's doc comment for why.)

  - `templateId` only (apply): the server resolves the named
    `OverallResultTemplate`'s CURRENT `content` itself — it never trusts a
    client-supplied content string for an apply — and snapshots that content
    for this parameter, alongside `templateId` (so the UI can show which
    template is active for it). 404 `OVERALL_RESULT_TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND` if
    the id doesn't resolve to an active template in this tenant.

    ```json
    { "templateId": "{{overallResultTemplateId}}" }
    ```

  - `content` only (edit): overwrites this parameter's applied content in
    place (post-apply technician edits, e.g. filling in a value the
    template left blank). `templateId` is left untouched, so the UI still
    shows which template this parameter started from even after the edited
    content diverges from that template's own current text.

    ```json
    { "content": "<p>Overall result: Normal.</p>" }
    ```

  Sending BOTH `templateId` and `content` in the same request, or NEITHER,
  is rejected with 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` — exactly one of the two is
  required per call.

  Gated by `TechnicianSetting.isOverallResultEditable` (default `false`,
  see "Technician Settings" module). When the toggle is off, this is a
  **silent no-op**: the request succeeds (200) but returns this parameter's
  current, unchanged overall result — it does NOT reject the request. Turn
  the toggle on first if a write doesn't seem to be taking effect.

  Response shape: `{ "resultParamId": string, "templateId": string | null,
  "content": string | null }` — this parameter's overall result state after
  the write (or after the no-op, if the toggle is off).

  ⚠️ Updated 2026-09-22: `resultParamId` MUST be one of this report's own
  result parameters — a smoke test found any arbitrary UUID would silently
  create its own orphaned row (returned in `overallResults` with no
  corresponding entry in `resultParams`). A `resultParamId` that doesn't
  belong to this report's test/panel is now rejected with 400
  `VALIDATION_ERROR` ("resultParamId does not belong to this report's
  test"), checked before the apply/edit body validation above. A real
  parameter with nothing ever applied still returns `{ "resultParamId":
  "...", "templateId": null, "content": null }`, not a 404 — only an
  unrelated/non-existent id is rejected.

  ⚠️ Known gap (tracked, not yet fixed): unlike every other mutating action
  on this report, this endpoint does NOT check `LabReportStatus` — a
  PUBLISHED report's overall result can still be edited through this route.
  The only guard that applies is the lock check below. Do not rely on
  publish-immutability for this one field yet.

  404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other-tenant/other-branch. 409
  `LAB_REPORT_LOCKED` if the report is locked (`lock()`'d via
  `POST /lab-reports/:id/lock`) — this is the only lifecycle gate currently
  enforced here.

  Requires `LAB_EDIT_REPORT` (unlike this module's read-only
  `GET /overall-result-templates*` routes, which are open to any
  authenticated business user with the Technician module enabled).
}
